{"title":"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Problems 8, 9 and 10 use the data found in the accompanying paragraph and figures\n</p><p>Four friends, Art, Roger, Paul and Trisha, bake cookies, and all cookies have the same thickness. The shapes of the cookies differ, as shown.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Art's cookies are trapezoids: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30c19e251320f614c89dd05c7666eb4b5b8eb84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(5,0)--(5,3)--(2,3)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((5,3), (5,0), origin)); label(&quot;5 in&quot;, (2.5,0), S); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (5,1.5), E); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (3.5,3), N);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Roger's cookies are rectangles: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffcf7138f4fa79b3d3030ad4a0e82a3a03322bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(4,0)--(4,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((4,2), (4,0), origin)); draw(rightanglemark((0,2), origin, (4,0))); label(&quot;4 in&quot;, (2,0), S); label(&quot;2 in&quot;, (4,1), E);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Paul's cookies are parallelograms: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7278165b0333733d86c18cdd642361a580edc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(3,0)--(2.5,2)--(-0.5,2)--cycle); draw((2.5,2)--(2.5,0), dashed); draw(rightanglemark((2.5,2),(2.5,0), origin)); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (1.5,0), S); label(&quot;2 in&quot;, (2.5,1), W);[/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> Trisha's cookies are triangles: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da492eba3c75cd91135085acf373c1215d7f5b48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));defaultpen(fontsize(8)); draw(origin--(3,0)--(3,4)--cycle); draw(rightanglemark((3,4),(3,0), origin)); label(&quot;3 in&quot;, (1.5,0), S); label(&quot;4 in&quot;, (3,2), E);[/asy]\" width=\"122\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p>Each friend uses the same amount of dough, and Art makes exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cookies. Art's cookies sell for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents each. To earn the same amount from a single batch, how much should one of Roger's cookies cost in cents?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e570682a1374d982afeb4e82a5bbc0ca7752ed02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 25\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 75\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of one of Art's cookies is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f61f2cea25a0dca8ff4d177b8cf597a8ef36f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 3 + \\frac{2 \\cdot 3}{2}=9+3=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" />. As he has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cookies in a batch, the amount of dough each person used is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327f90a4ad16078743c5bda51bd7068c23b526c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot 12=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" />. Roger's cookies have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410b09eda800c7d697513c3e9233396b6ded65bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{2 \\cdot 4}=\\frac{144}{8}= 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"37\" /> cookies in  a batch. In total, the amount of money Art will earn is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7b78b98dadb73bcc2d944492a772219bb35c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot 60=720$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the amount Roger would need to charge per cookie is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6773f680ec225abccad0ad4213f889b667a3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{720}{18}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8\">2003 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <